{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Eleven days from Horev.</b> It abbreviates the matter, for it is stated: eleven days' journey that they made from Horev until the sending of the spies from Kadesh Barnea — for from the day HaShem swore that they would not enter the land, no commandment was renewed except in the fortieth year." "<b>Eleven days.</b> Defective in bet, as if written באחד עשר יום. Examples: ״כי ששת ימים עשה ה׳ את השמים״ etc.; ״אם הגד תגידו אותו לי שבעת ימי המשתה״ in Judges; ״הזעק לי את איש יהודה שלשת ימים״ in Samuel; and many more." "<b>Eleven days.</b> Rashi said: Moses said to them, etc., that they traversed the entire route in three days. What Rashi explained is not to teach us the three encampments by the days, for one does not count from the twentieth of Iyar until the twenty-ninth of Sivan but thirty-eight days; rather, it comes to teach us that they did not travel from the twentieth of Iyar until the twenty-ninth of Sivan but in three encampments. The first encampment is Kivrot HaTa'avah, where they spent thirty full days — nine of Iyar and twenty-one of Sivan; subtract from them the second encampment, which is Hatzerot, where they spent eight full days and part of the twenty-ninth of Sivan. And the third encampment is Kadesh Barnea, which was on the twenty-ninth of Sivan, from which they sent the spies, as I explained in the perasha of BeHa'alotekha."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The phrase ועוד צא מהם is rendered hyper-literally; it likely means 'subtract from them' in the calendrical calculation, but the syntax is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:17.541479355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}